{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1420,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As far as we know, time only moves in one\ndirection – forward – but if you could"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6050,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "loop back to visit the universe at an earlier\npoint in time, a famous paradox arises."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10460,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What if you killed your grandfather when he\nwas a child?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13360,
    "dDurationMs": 3659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then your father or mother wouldn't have been\nborn, so you wouldn't have been born, so you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17019,
    "dDurationMs": 4651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wouldn't have been able to go back in time\nto kill your grandfather in the first place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21670,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Paradox."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22670,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The simplest resolution to the grandfather\nparadox is that when you go back in time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26220,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're actually not going back into your own\nhistory but to a copy, and everything you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29830,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do there influences the new alternate future\nof that universe, not your own past."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34440,
    "dDurationMs": 2899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's boring, because it just avoids\nthe paradox."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37339,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If what you do when you go back in time actually\ninfluences your own past, and the effects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41609,
    "dDurationMs": 5270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of your time travel do loop back to the present...future...past\n– no problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46879,
    "dDurationMs": 4731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's just follow the paradoxical timeline\nthrough BEYOND its paradoxical conclusion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51610,
    "dDurationMs": 4049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You go back in time, kill your grandfather,\nthus you aren't born so you can't go back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55659,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in time, thus your grandfather isn't killed,\nthus you are born, so you go back in time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60229,
    "dDurationMs": 2031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and kill your grandfather, and so on..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62260,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm showing this as a linear series of events\nbut really it's two entangled histories happening"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67140,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in parallel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68570,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is that even possible?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69570,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, I don't know about the time travel part,\nbut subatomic particles regularly do multiple"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74130,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "different things in parallel – it's called\nquantum superposition and is responsible for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77610,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the weirdness of the double slit experiment,\nmany properties of atoms and molecules, fusion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81820,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the sun's core, and so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83930,
    "dDurationMs": 4119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if the universe were to exist in a superposition\nof two states – your grandfather is alive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88049,
    "dDurationMs": 3771,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and your grandfather is dead – then the\nnatural result is a superposition of two states:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91820,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're born and able to go back in time to\nkill your grandfather, and you're not born."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96010,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the natural result of these is a superposition\nof two states – your grandfather is dead"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100630,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and your grandfather is alive – and so,\nat least from a logical perspective, this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104650,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "looping timeline is entirely consistent and\nthere's no paradox."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108350,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a similar paradox-free solution can be\nobtained by viewing the problem as a steady-state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112000,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "solution to a Markov chain – but I won't\ngo into that here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114840,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now of course nothing about these solutions\nto the grandfather paradox suggests that closed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118820,
    "dDurationMs": 3509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time loops are actually possible – in fact,\nsome of the implications this kind of time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122329,
    "dDurationMs": 3771,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "loop have in the study of complexity theory\nseem to suggest that time loops – and thus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126100,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time travel into the past – must be impossible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129360,
    "dDurationMs": 4099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the main point is sometimes we think a\nsituation creates a paradox when it doesn't,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133459,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and really the only paradox is how our thinking\ncan be twisted enough to dream up time-traveling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138489,
    "dDurationMs": 27771,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "murderous grandsons, but not twisted enough\nto think about twisting time."
    } ]
  } ]
}
